---
# The SteamCMD install only. The config claim is created by k8s/volume-claim, which must own
# it — it renders and applies that PVC itself before the workload exists, so declaring it
# here too would give two roles the same object.
#
# Named server-pvc.yaml, not pvc.yaml: volume-claim stages ITS claim as
# manifests/valheim/pvc.yaml, and k8s/manifests renders every manifests_files entry into that
# same directory. Under the shorter name the two writers overwrote each other on every deploy,
# the render read as changed, and the rollout-restart gate took the server down each time
# (#1550). ENFORCED by ansible/tests/k8s/test_volume_claim_pvc_path_collision.py.
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ valheim_k8s_server_claim }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  # nobackup: every byte here is re-downloadable from Steam, and B2 is the scarce resource.
  storageClassName: {{ valheim_k8s_server_storage_class }}
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: {{ valheim_k8s_server_size }}
